2026-09-22 23:53:14,575 | INFO | [congress-pelosi-v3] [agents][tool_call 3] remember_risk_note: text=Bear case against copying the visible book for congress-pelosi-v3: \n 1. Stale Filings / Look-Ahead & Reporting Lag: Under the STOCK Act, public disclosures can take weeks or months to be filed. Furthermore, as shown by the PTR filings (20033725, 20034836, 20035143), signature/report dates fall after the current as_of date (2026-01-22), meaning no valid public transactions are available as of the execution date. Trying to copy trades based on delayed disclosures exposes the strategy to severe look-ahead bias and buying at stale, unfavorable market prices after the initial move has already occurred. \n 2. Wide Bid-Ask Spreads & Liquidity Gaps: Congressional disclosures often feature large-cap options or less liquid LEAPs and specific strike selections. Copying exact trades without real-time liquidity analysis can result in severe slippage, wide bid-ask spreads, and poor execution quality. \n 3. Information Asymmetry & Absence of Intent: Public filings disclose aggregated ranges (e.g., $50,001 - $100,000) rather than exact share quantities, entry prices, or exit strategies. Blindly mimicking these trades ignores portfolio context, diversification needs, risk tolerance, and hedging activities (e.g., whether a trade is part of a spread or a macro hedge). \n 4. Conclusion: No orders were submitted. The bear case firmly supports doing nothing due to stale/unavailable filings and structural replication risks.
